proposed_comments.body:
### Keep tray setup running when theme monitoring fails

**Severity:** `medium`

`ThemeListener` starts WMI watchers and can throw when theme monitoring is unavailable. This new construction runs during `FrmScreen_Load` before cursor setup and `UpdateNotifyIcon()`, so letting the exception reach the outer catch skips the rest of that initialization. The settings reload path also calls this method on the UI thread.

Catch and log construction failure locally, then return so the caller continues with the currently selected icon. This matches the existing fail-open behavior used by the Peek caller.

```suggestion
            try
            {
                themeListener = new ManagedCommon.ThemeListener();
            }
            catch (Exception e)
            {
                Logger.Log(e);
                return;
            }
```
